# ⏱️ Complexity Analysis

Understanding complexity is an important part of solving DSA problems.

### Time Complexity

Time complexity describes how the running time of an algorithm grows with input size.

Common complexities:

```text
O(1)       → Constant
O(log n)   → Logarithmic
O(n)       → Linear
O(n log n) → Linearithmic
O(n²)      → Quadratic
O(2ⁿ)      → Exponential
O(n!)      → Factorial
```

### Space Complexity

Space complexity describes the additional memory required by an algorithm.

Example:

```cpp
unordered_map<int, int> mp;
```

The hash map may require additional memory proportional to the number of elements.

Therefore:

```text
Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(n)
```

